    P("engulfing-switch", "Engulfing Switch", "Nison bullish/bearish engulfing reversal switch", "pattern", ["steve-nison", "thomas-bulkowski"], "D", FV.engulfing,
      "Buy after a bullish engulfing candle ends a decline; sell after a bearish engulfing candle ends a rally. An engulfing candle's body swallows the whole body of the day before.",
      ["Bullish engulfing: after a decline, a down day (close below open) is followed by an up day that opens at or below the prior close and closes at or above the prior open.",
       "Bearish engulfing: after a rise, an up day is followed by a down day that opens at or above the prior close and closes at or below the prior open.",
       "In at the close of a bullish engulfing day. Out at the close of a bearish engulfing day. Otherwise the rule keeps its last call."],
      ["A decline (or rise) means the prior close is below (or above) the close 5 sessions before it. Nison and Bulkowski require a prior trend but give no number.",
       "Nison weighs support, resistance and confirmation, which a mechanical rule cannot judge. No confirmation day is required here.",
       "Shadows are ignored, as both Nison and Bulkowski allow. One edge of the new body may equal the old body's edge, as in the TA-Lib pattern library, but not both.",
       "Crypto trades around the clock, so a coin's daily open is just the prior close. For coins the open is taken as the prior close, and the pattern becomes a close beyond the prior day's open."],
      "Japanese Candlestick Charting Techniques (1991); statistics in Encyclopedia of Candlestick Charts (2008)",
      sources=[("ThePatternSite: Bullish Engulfing (identification and statistics)", "https://www.thepatternsite.com/BullEngulfing.html"),
               ("ThePatternSite: Bearish Engulfing (identification and statistics)", "https://thepatternsite.com/BearEngulfing.html"),
               ("StockCharts ChartSchool: Candlestick bullish reversal patterns", "https://chartschool.stockcharts.com/table-of-contents/chart-analysis/candlestick-charts/candlestick-bullish-reversal-patterns")]),
    P("hikkake", "Hikkake", "Chesler's hikkake (inside-day false breakout) switch", "pattern", ["daniel-chesler"], "D", FV.hikkake,
      "When a stock breaks down out of an inside day and then reverses back above the inside day's high within 3 days, buy the reversal that traps the sellers.",
      ["Setup: an inside day (a lower high and a higher low than the day before), then a day with a lower high and a lower low than the inside day (bullish) or a higher high and a higher low (bearish).",
       "In at the close if, within 3 sessions after a bullish setup, a close is above the inside day's high. The stop is the lowest low of the pattern.",
       "Out at the close if a close falls below that stop, or if a bearish setup is confirmed by a close below the inside day's low within 3 sessions."],
      ["Chesler enters during the day when price crosses the inside day's high. On daily bars the close must clear it.",
       "Chesler gives no profit target, so a trade ends only at the stop or on an opposite hikkake.",
       "If a newer setup forms, it replaces the older one."],
      "Daniel Chesler, 'Trading False Moves with the Hikkake Pattern', Active Trader (April 2004)",
      sources=[("Chesler, 'Trading False Moves with the Hikkake Pattern', Active Trader (April 2004), PDF", "https://c.mql5.com/forextsd/forum/34/hikkake.pdf"),
               ("Wikipedia: Hikkake pattern", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hikkake_pattern")]),
    P("turtle-soup-plus-one", "Turtle Soup Plus One", "Raschke & Connors' Turtle Soup Plus One (failed 20-day breakdown)", "pattern",
      ["linda-bradford-raschke", "larry-connors"], "D", FV.turtle_soup,
      "Buy when a stock closes at a new 20-day low and climbs back above the old low the next day, betting the breakdown was a trap. It turns the Turtles' breakout rule on its head.",
      ["Day 1: the close is below the lowest low of the prior 20 sessions, and that low was set at least 3 sessions earlier.",
       "Day 2: in at the close if the close is back above that old 20-day low.",
       "Out at the close if a close falls below the lower of the day-1 and day-2 lows (the stop), or after 6 sessions in the trade."],
      ["The book buys during day 2 with a stop order at the old low. On daily bars the close must be above it.",
       "The book takes partial profits within 2 to 6 bars and trails a stop on the rest. A 6-session time exit stands in for both.",
       "The original Turtle Soup (same-day entry, old low at least 4 days back) is the sister pattern. Plus One is used because it waits for a closing confirmation.",
       "The authors also sell short failed breakouts to new highs. Be The Puck tests only the long side."],
      "Street Smarts: High Probability Short-Term Trading Strategies (1995)",
      sources=[("QuantNet forum: Turtle Soup Plus One rules quoted from Street Smarts", "https://quantnet.com/threads/need-vba-help-for-trading-tool.2769/latest"),
               ("MQL5: 'Turtle Soup' and 'Turtle Soup Plus One' formalised from Street Smarts", "https://www.mql5.com/tr/articles/2717"),
               ("Traders.com (Working Money, 2005): Pezzutti, 'Short-Term Patterns: Turtle Soup'", "https://technical.traders.com/tradersonline/display.asp?art=2414")]),

